  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consultancy for following up of CAFOD Partnerships and Activities in Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD has been working with church, Caritas Internationalis agencies and civil society organisations since the early 2000s.  The work has involved providing funding and technical support to partner led one-off and long term activities focused at alleviating poverty, promoting peace and reconciliation, public accountability and transparency, accompaniment to build the capacity of church partners and local communities; implementation of HIV &amp; AIDS and sustainable livelihoods.   The management of the CAFOD partnerships and programme/projects in Angola was coordinated by the Regional Manager for West Africa and Great Lakes based in CAFOD London office. With the decentralisation of CAFOD operations to the regions and political evolution in Angola, CAFOD has shifted the Angola programme from the West Africa and Great lakes region to Southern Africa region. The responsibility to manage the partnerships and programmes has been passed to Southern Africa regional team in Harare. The actual handover the management responsibility was done at the end of 2007. A Consultant has therefore been hired to follow up CAFOD partnerships and activities in Angola and compile a report to the requirements of CAFOD.</narrative>
  </description>
